    {
        id shell-as-library
        title "Make nsh a shell library with a binary frontend, per [dec:nsh:shell-as-library]"
        priority 0
        kind @refactor
        children (
            {
                id host-owns-streams
                title "The shell's three streams come from the frontend, not descriptors 0/1/2"
                priority 0
                kind @feat
                sealed true
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-08-07T09:11:54.770587255Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-08-07T09:33:13.662151863Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
                    }
                )
            }

            {
                id errors-are-values
                title "Replace the longjmp-as-unwind exception mechanism with Result propagation"
                priority 0
                kind @refactor
                deps (delete-memalloc sanctioned-divergences public-api-design)
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-08-12T12:48:34.059347929Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
                    }
                )
            }

            {
                id no-ambient-state
                title "Move every process-global static into a shell instance; no globals, no thread-locals"
                priority 0
                kind @refactor
                deps (errors-are-values sanctioned-divergences public-api-design)
                children (
                    {
                        id thread-context
                        title "Thread a context parameter through every function that touches a static"
                        priority 0
                        kind @refactor
                        deps (errors-are-values public-api-design)
                    }

                    {
                        id move-state
                        title "Move each static table onto the shell instance, one table per commit"
                        priority 0
                        kind @refactor
                        deps (thread-context)
                    }
                )
            }

            {
                id host-owns-signals
                title "The frontend claims signal dispositions; needs pty cases for job control first"
                priority 0
                kind @refactor
                deps (no-ambient-state)
            }

            {
                id owned-data
                title "Delete memalloc: the shell's data becomes owned Rust values, per [dec:nsh:owned-data]"
                priority 0
                kind @refactor
                children (
                    {
                        id owned-nodes
                        title "union node becomes an owned Rust enum; copyfunc becomes Rc + Clone"
                        priority 0
                        kind @refactor
                        sealed true
                        log (
                            {
                                at 2026-08-07T09:34:17.049858598Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @status
                                text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-08-07T11:42:00.055092499Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @status
                                text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
                            }
                        )
                    }

                    {
                        id owned-strings
                        title "The stack string builder becomes an owned byte vector across parser and expand"
                        priority 0
                        kind @refactor
                        deps (owned-nodes sanctioned-divergences)
                        sealed true
                        log (
                            {
                                at 2026-08-08T10:06:34.731197116Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "Partial on wt/owned-strings (858a6e2..f6b5c15), left Todo on purpose. String-builder call sites 205 -> 91. Cleared: parser.rs (74 -> 8, and the 8 are getmbc/dollarsq_escape writing through a raw cursor into a Vec's spare capacity, plus expandstr's read of expand.rs's builder), nodes.rs NodeText, cd.rs, histedit.rs, mystring.rs, exec.rs, jobs.rs, eval.rs, shellmain.rs, mail.rs. Remaining: expand.rs 41, bltin/printf.rs 22, miscbltin.rs 8, var.rs 7 (listvars' envp array), output.rs 3, redir.rs 1, input.rs 1. expand.rs is blocked structurally, not by effort: expmeta borrows the global expdest to encode directory entries into the glob buffer, so expdest cannot become an index into one owned buffer until memtodest/chtodest/mbtodest take their destination as a parameter. plan/decisions/owned-data.md has the full reasoning. Unconverted rider from docs/std-replacements.md §3 step 3: cd.rs:234,253 libc::strtok -> split_str(b\"/\") filtered for empty fields."
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-08-08T11:36:13.916688376Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @status
                                text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-08-08T12:20:57.234138379Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "Partial on wt/owned-strings2 (907d761, 5149923), still Doing. expand.rs's expansion buffer is owned: expdest is the length of a static BString, memtodest/strtodest/cvtnum take &mut BString, and grabstackstr(expdest) is a copy into the region -- the seam with delete-memalloc, since ifsbreakup/expandmeta/strlist are still stalloc'd C structs. String-builder sites: expand.rs 42 -> 16, redir.rs 1 -> 0. Of the 16 left in expand.rs, six are the glob buffer (expmeta's growstackto/stnputs and addfnamealt's grabstackstr/stackblock/stnputs), four are the stackblock()/grabstackstr macro transcriptions it needs, and six are the owned buffer's own helpers, which touch no region. crate::memalloc:: in expand.rs 28 -> 23: five string builder (all glob), one the grabstackstr seam, eight stalloc/ckmalloc for strlist/ifsregion/wcifs and _rmescapes' HEAP arm, nine stack marks. Not converted: expand.rs's glob buffer (now separable -- expmeta's memtodest output is scratch that stnputs overwrites, so it moved to its own buffer), bltin/printf.rs 26 (print_escape_str formats a run of X's through xasprintf and memcpies the real bytes over them, three cursors into one region), miscbltin.rs 8 (readcmd, shares the ifsbreakup/strlist seam), parser.rs 8 (getmbc/dollarsq_escape writing into a BString's spare capacity), var.rs 4 and output.rs 3 and input.rs 1. var.rs and alias.rs were off-limits this pass -- another agent is converting those tables to BTreeMap. Five load-bearing sites written up on plan/decisions/owned-data.md, the sharpest being that _rmescapes leaves expdest pointing into a ckmalloc'd block expandmeta then frees, and that expandarg(n, NULL, flag) has two readers outside expand.c (redir.c:openhere and parser.c:expandstr) -- missing the second costs the \"+ \" on every set -x line. crates/nsh/tests/expansion_buffer.rs is new: four cases pinning what the differential corpus cannot aim at, per docs/idiomatization.md §5. Both commits fully gated: PASS=61498 FAIL=0 XFAIL=0, POSIX 54/657 against the C's 56/655 with the same two differentials, ptydiff 31/0, register 13/13."
                            }

